name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-preassessment-q4_2026'

question 'A student asks AI to wire up a "Like" button. The AI confidently returns code that uses `document.getElementById("likeBtn")`. The page actually has a button with id `like-btn`. What kind of AI failure is this?'

right 'Context blindness — AI guessed an id based on patterns from similar pages, not from this page.'
wrong 'A syntax error AI should have caught.'
wrong 'A browser compatibility bug.'
wrong 'A network issue with the AI service.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

